@RobertMeisner you would not do that, you would first check if data is valid and the fetch the property. Two versions:

``` php
if ($article->author !== null) {
  $pk = $article->author->id;
}
```

``` php
if (!$article->author->isNullObject()) {
  $pk = $article->author->id;
}
```

it's fine as long as u can simply do

``` php
 if ($article->author){
$pk = $article->author->id;
}
```
